prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept. A restrained architectural illustration on a genuinely transparent background for a personal website.

IMAGE 1 IS THE PRIMARY REFERENCE: Kyoto Station viewed upward from beside its monumental stair. Preserve this specific architectural composition and its identifying features. IMAGE 2 is contextual reference of the same Kyoto Station atrium, for understanding the curved lattice canopy; do not copy its crowded detail or its straight corridor viewpoint.

Draw a simplified but RECOGNIZABLY KYOTO STATION illustration, from the stair-side viewpoint of IMAGE 1:
- the dramatic, very long grand staircase rises diagonally up toward the LEFT inside the composition;
- the inclined escalator band follows it;
- preserve the conspicuous tilted hollow SQUARE FRAME beside the staircase, but make its red color very pale dusty terracotta;
- the high enclosed SKYBRIDGE crosses the upper composition horizontally/diagonally as in image 1;
- behind it, the characteristic sweeping steel-and-glass curved lattice roof / wall meets the stepped mirrored block massing. Preserve its distinctive contour and broad geometric organization;
- retain the monumental open central space, layered terraces and angular wall massing. This must read as the particular Kyoto Station stair/atrium view, NOT a generic glass office corridor.

Style: a sophisticated flat architectural collage with a little translucent depth, thin clean outlines, broad softly tinted glass planes. Simplify repeated details into a COARSE structural grid (approximately 6 by 8 large cells, single lines with NO nested bracing). Keep the architecturally distinctive silhouettes and the square frame. Remove railings, people, signage, billboards, lights, tiny windows, floor seams, photographic textures, and complex realistic shading. Staircase indicated with around a dozen fine step lines, not hundreds. Smooth pale material, not photographic realism, not shiny plastic or a toy model.

Composition: widescreen 16:9. Put a coherent stair-and-atrium composition across the right 65% of the image, with the large staircase, tilted square and skybridge visually legible within that region. Leftmost 35% is empty transparent space for website text. Main architecture occupies the upper and middle-right; softly dissolve lower edges into alpha. Do not extend a huge opaque building wall into the left reading area.
Palette: very pale cool silver #c8d6de, frosted ice-blue #c6dce8, off-white translucent planes; only one small very muted pale terracotta square as in the real reference. Low contrast, airy and transparent, no strong dark areas.
ACTUAL transparent background with alpha. No white rectangle. No text, logo, watermark, vegetation or invented decorative geometry.
Goal: keep the RECOGNIZABLE ARCHITECTURAL FEATURES and composition of this real Kyoto Station view, while achieving simplicity by removing small detail and reducing contrast.
